From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:06:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: free the CeUtils completion event before tearing down
 its channel

With completion callbacks enabled (the sysmem scrubber's CeUtils),
_memmgrMemUtilsScrubInitRegisterCallback() registers a
NV2080_NOTIFIERS_FIFO_EVENT_MTHD nonstall event whose callback,
_ceutilsSemaphoreEventCallback(), reads the finish payload semaphore and
runs the completion callbacks. That event fires for any channel's nonstall
interrupt and is delivered from the lockless nonstall bottom half.

ceutilsDestruct() ends the USERD, pushbuffer and notifier mappings and
clears pFinishPayloadSemaMemDesc before it frees the client, and with it
the event. A nonstall interrupt from any other channel in that window runs
the callback against the torn-down channel state.

Free the event right after the final completion processing, before the
teardown. Freeing a nonstall event waits for notifications already in
progress, so no callback runs after that point. Only the SoCs with sysmem
compression create a sysmem scrubber.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mem_mgr/ce_utils.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mem_mgr/ce_utils.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mem_mgr/ce_utils.c
index 1be22271..cd6088ea 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mem_mgr/ce_utils.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mem_mgr/ce_utils.c
@@ -440,6 +440,17 @@ ceutilsDestruct_IMPL
     // make sure no new work was queued from callbacks
     NV_ASSERT(pCeUtils->lastCompletedPayload == lastSubmittedPayload);
 
+    //
+    // The completion callback runs from the nonstall interrupt path for any
+    // channel's FIFO_EVENT_MTHD, without locks, and reads the finish payload
+    // semaphore. Free its event before tearing down the channel mappings
+    // below; freeing a nonstall event waits for notifications in flight.
+    //
+    if (pCeUtils->bCompletionCallbackEnabled)
+    {
+        NV_ASSERT_OK(pRmApi->Free(pRmApi, pChannel->hClient, pChannel->eventId));
+    }
+
     if ((pChannel->bClientUserd) && (pChannel->pControlGPFifo != NULL))
     {
         if (kbusIsBarAccessBlocked(GPU_GET_KERNEL_BUS(pGpu)))
